Maya: RFC follow-up: lightweight offline escrow-watchdog proposal. Goal: safe, auditable promotion of fallback sealed keys in air-gapped onprem bundles with minimal operator friction.
Alyssa: summary: watchdog runs in-cluster, no external network calls, enforces full-manifest verification, two-phase tombstone/GC, and a configurable commit policy (observe -> commit).
Noah: restriction: never call customer KMS or key services. All crypto ops must use keys present in the bundle or operator-managed cluster keys.
Devon: reconcile sketch (pseudo):
```go
