```
Tess: ops UX: add bundle-local CLI `rundown` with `list`, `promote --force --sigs`, `restore-tombstone`. `--force` requires two operator signatures by default. No network.
Maya: GC flow: soft tombstone (retain blobs for RETENTION_DAYS, default 14d) -> hard GC after retention. Soft tombstone reversible.
Noah: security: default mode = observe-only for airgapped installs. WATCHDOG_MODE = [disabled|observe-only|auto|emergency]. Auto requires REQUIRED_SEATS_FOR_AUTO threshold.
Devon: logging: append-only local audit log with structured lines: timestamp | actor | action | id | fingerprint | reason. Keep immutable counters for sequence proof.
Tess: rollout: disabled on initial canary; enable observe-only for 30d on canaries; after analysis opt into auto/quorum per site. Playbook: how to respond to canary-promote-fail -> check `rundown list` -> coordinate manual promote with two seats -> `rundown promote --force`.
Alyssa: testing: unit tests for reconcile branches, e2e harness that runs offline in a tiny k8s cluster, chaos test with concurrent canary apply and watchdog run.
Noah: open items: operator key rotation in offline mode (follow-up thread), retention window tuning, and telemetry opt-in shape for hosted customers (airgapped silent).
Maya: action items: Tess write playbook + CLI spec, Devon add unit+e2e harness, Noah add threat-model notes, Alyssa update RFC doc with audit record format and default configs.
deploy-bot: canary deploy: operator-watchdog v1 -> onprem-canary-7 :rocket: logs:/var/log/operator-watchdog/2026-03-24.log
